{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 58, :comments ["<b>If you do not take care to do all the words of this Torah written in this book, to fear this glorious and awesome Name.</b> This verse explains that the intention of all the commandments in the Torah is a single goal, and it is fear (of HaShem). And so Moses explained at the holy assembly that the ultimate intention in the giving of the Torah was nothing but fear, as he said (Exodus 20:17): ״לבעבור נסות אתכם בא האלהים ובעבור תהיה יראתו על פניכם״ — 'in order to test you the Elohim came, and in order that His fear be upon your faces.' From this King Solomon saw and did likewise, sealing his book with it. And they further said (Isaiah 33:6): ״יראת ה' היא אוצרו״ — 'the fear of YHWH is His treasure'; if there is fear of YHWH, yes; if not, no. The plain sense of the verse: the fear of YHWH is laid up in His supreme and beloved treasure, in that He sets reward upon it. Or one may say: the fear of YHWH, which is among those who fear Him, is His treasure that He stores away for them. And the reason Scripture used the language of 'treasure' regarding fear is that it is not in the hand of the King to make a treasure unless He gathers wealth from others, and what He gathers and stores in particular is called a treasure — and so fear is not in the hands of Heaven (to bestow), and therefore He calls it a treasure. From this you learn that fear is the essence of everything, and it is greater than all other traits, and it surpasses all the commandments. For the other commandments, such as tefillin and tzitzit and the like, have a set time for their performance; once one has finished performing them, he is released from them. Not so the commandment of fear, for it has no designated time but endures forever, at every moment and every hour; as it is written (Psalms 19:10): ״יראת ה' טהורה עומדת לעד״ — 'the fear of YHWH is pure, standing forever' — unlike the other commandments, which are completed after their performance at a fixed time. And fear has no perfection except through deeds; this is what it says: 'if you do not take care to do' — to be scrupulous regarding negative commandments and to fulfill positive commandments."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:52.625713959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}